WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.710
John: Good morning Hank, it's Wednesdaaaaaaay,
it's Pizzamas!

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.799
We've just come from the Save the Children
Gala.

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:09.580
Hank: I met Jennifer Garner.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.690
J: That was weird but she seemed cool.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.790
H: and I stood nearby Olivia Wilde.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.870
J: It could be a Gala or a gah-lah.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.880
H: Do you want to answer some questions that
people --

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.880
J: YES!

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:20.880
H: -- just sent in?

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.140
John Green, what is your opinion on lamps?

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.710
J: I am opposed to them.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.240
H: I love lamp.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.820
Debate over the best kind of chocolate: white,
milk, or dark.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.980
J: I don't know that this is going to be a
debate but I actually have a very strong opinion,

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.480
so let's just do this 1 2 3.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.550
One, two, three!

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.620
Both together: Dark!

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.059
J: Oh thank god!

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:41.260
Because we were about to not be brothers anymore.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.329
H: Will there ever be dear Hank and John merch?

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:45.930
J: That's what the world's missing is dear
Hank and John merch.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.969
You know what kind of merch we DO have?

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:49.300
Pizza John merch is available now.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.300
H: Eeeeh.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.410
Only for a couple more days.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.109
J: At DFTBA.com.

00:00:54.109 --> 00:00:58.219
Pizzamas merch, it's like suits... but mostly
T-shirts and shoelaces.

00:00:58.219 --> 00:00:59.219
H: Actually, you know what I was wearing underneath
the whole time--

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:00.219
J: Ooooh!

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:02.010
H: during the Save the Children gala.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.750
J: He likes to keep me close to his heart.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.750
H: John --

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.750
J: Yeah.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.110
H: -- Do your best impression of your favorite
dinosaur.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.260
J: We don't know what dinosaurs sounded like.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.470
H: [disappointed exhale]

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:13.680
J: It's true!

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.680
[squawk]

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.680
H: Ok.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.680
Ok.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.680
J: Might be.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.640
H: I'm glad you-- at least you made a noise.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.240
J: That was a diplodocus.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.240
My favorite dinosaur.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.380
But we don't know if that's what they sounded
like [retching] we don't know!

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:31.560
We have no way of knowing [retching] we have
no way of knowing.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.560
[screeching]

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.110
H: maybe they just like, sounded like humans.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:41.800
They were just like [babbling] Like that dog
from that thing on Tumblr.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.240
[impersonating human dog]

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.869
J: Rosianna took away my Tumblr password,
so I don't know what's happening on Tumblr

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:47.869
anymore

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:48.869
H: [gibberish]

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:49.869
J: Sounds funny.

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:50.869
H: It's pretty funny.

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:51.869
J: Why did you take away my Tumblr password?

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:53.619
There are so many lovely things happening.

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:54.619
H: [gibberish]

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:57.240
J: Nicole's question is "What are your holiday
traditions?

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.729
H: Saying what we're thankful for.

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:02.020
J: Oh, our mom always puts tremendous pressure
on us

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.020
H: There is a great deal of pressure

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.369
J: To come up with like a new thing that we're
thankful for.

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:10.690
So if I say like I'm thankful for my kids,
Mom will always say "No no no no no, you said

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.820
that in 2011."

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:16.060
[Hank laughs] Then I'll have to think of something
new that I'm thankful for.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.290
And I'm 38, you know?

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:20.890
That's 38 years of having to be grateful.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.460
H: Yeah, you gotta take like individual foods.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.650
[John laughs] Like "this year I'm thankful
for green beans!"

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.010
J: God, I'm so grateful for cranberries.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.840
Where would we be without them as a species?

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.220
H: Yeah, right.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.920
Yeah, exactly the same place, but where would
cranberries be?

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.300
J: They would be dead.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.800
Like 40% of species, which we've eliminated
in the last 500 years, go team!

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.360
[Hank reluctantly high fives] Actually, no.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.090
That was... not an appropriate high five.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:51.740
H: Well, I mean 99.9% of species that have
existed no longer exist.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.470
J: Tight, but we've--

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.980
H: Usually not so rapidly.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.590
J: We've eliminated more in the last 400 years
than in the previous million.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:01.590
H: Yeah.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.050
Yeah, we're roughly on par with an asteroid.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.400
J: We are killin' it...

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.400
H: Oh!

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.400
J: Literally.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:14.670
Hank, can you please describe the meaning
of life from the perspective of a chicken?

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.230
H: [a startlingly accurate impression of a
chicken]

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.230
J: [giggles]

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.740
H: [continues to be good at being a chicken]

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.700
J: Hank, how did you and John meet your wives?

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.630
H: I met my wife, she lived across a, uh...

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:28.710
J: a desert!

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:29.980
[Hank laughs] A continent!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.290
H: hallway

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.040
J: An ocean!

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.980
H: From my dorm room.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.950
J: Alright, room service is here, we have
to go.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.950
Hank.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:38.950
H: Yes.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.310
J: Thank you for being awesome, I like your
tie by the way.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.370
H: You're welcome, I got it at Banana Republic.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.360
J: DFTBA, I will see you right now and also
tomorrow.

